# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the test suites of a sanitizer build
# (meson.build: test setup "sanitize", which `meson test` uses by itself in
# a build made with -Db_sanitize=address...). By hand:
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/lsan.supp build/<name>-test
#
# Only memory of libraries that LeakSanitizer cannot follow is listed.
# Nothing allocated by this tree's own code is.

# fontconfig: a pattern keeps its element array, and a value list its next
# entry, as an OFFSET from the object, not as a pointer (the same structures
# live in its mmap()ed cache files). LeakSanitizer finds no pointer to them
# and reports the elements of every pattern that is alive at exit - those
# of the configuration FcInit () loads on Pango's start-up thread, those in
# the caches of Pango's font map - as lost, with all that hangs off them.
# (What the text code allocates through fontconfig itself is given back in
# walpe_text_release (); a text-part check holds that against the heap.)
leak:libfontconfig.so
